<title>SWEDEN: POLL-SWEDISH MATCH H1 PROFIT SEEN HIGHER.</title>
<headline>POLL-SWEDISH MATCH H1 PROFIT SEEN HIGHER.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish Match was expected to post a pre-tax profit of 799 million crowns for the first half of 1997 against 572 million crowns a year ago, a Reuters poll of eight analysts found on Monday.</p>
<p>Forecasts varied between 742 and 898 million crowns.</p>
<p>For the full year the company was expected to post a profit of 1.78 billion crowns from 1.53 billion in 1996.</p>
<p>Analysts interviewed for the poll were from Carnegie, CI Nordic Securities, Enskilda, James Capel, Kleinwort Benson, Penser, Swedbank and Ohman.</p>
<p>Swedish Match will release its half year report on August 12.</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>PRE-TAX PROFIT (Mln skr)</p>
<p>		   AVG	RANGE	    NO OF ANALYSTS</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> H1 97	    799	742-898			 8</p>
<p> Full yr 97   1,781    1,691-1,942		     8</p>
<p> Full yr 98   1,915    1,715-2,261		     6</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>-- Kristina Zetterlund, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1005</p>
